>   Orcrist, and Sting are obvious, but Snickersnee I don't recognize.

	The criminal cried as he dropped him down
	In a state of wild alarm;
	With a fearful, frightful, frantic frown,
	I bared my big right arm!
	I seized him by his little pig-tail,
	And on his knees fell he--
	As he shivered and struggled, and gurgled and guggled,
	I drew my snickersnee!

	Ah, never shall I forget the cry, 
		or the shriek that shrieked he,
	As I gnashed my teeth, and from my sheath
		I drew my Snickersnee!

		--Koko, Lord high executioner of Titipu
		  (From Sir W.S. Gilbert's "The Mikado")

"Snickersnee" is, I believe, a Dutch word meaning 'knife' or 'sword'.
Koko refers to his "sabre true" (presumably a katana) as a snickersnee,
and the rest is history...
